title The walk and the listing -- a meter over the guards that read what git disowns
prompt autonomous loop, GRASS auditing lane; the card's own GRASS account named the next lap
rota lap 4670, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; read the threshold, the Lindy effect and the compass. The row asks what the work is FOR and listens for the page nobody answered. It named the lap: REDS %722 ended on a sentence nobody had answered -- twelve more tree-rooted walks stand unprobed -- and Lindy said a meter over the class outlives twelve hand probes.
think Cold roster first. A pass launched 23:51 by the previous lap already held the lock and was measuring this HEAD, so I held still and read while it ran rather than opening a second (%359). It closed 270 run, 267 green, 1 red, 2 gated, tree_moved=no.
think The red is dated_path at cadence tier, last run 20260910.022254 -- %626's parked refs_lost, which the card already names as Keaton's, since a roster gate word reads custody gates alone. Nothing of mine to close.
think My own front named twelve unprobed tree-rooted find scans. A hand probe buys twelve answers and leaves the thirteenth walk unmeasured, which is exactly how the two that fired arrived. So I read the class instead.
think Measured the population three spellings deep before trusting one, because %721 recorded that same census being a claim about a spelling three times. Command-position find, first operand after leading -L/-H/-P, root resolved against the tracked listing.
think Three guards caught faults in my own new work before it shipped, which is what a hot pass is for. shell_dialect walled xargs -a as a GNU extension, so the list is read on stdin and a whitespace-carrying path now refuses by name rather than being split into names that open nothing. instrument_refusal caught git status --ignored piped under || true, which would have handed exposure an empty list and printed every walk as latent under exposed=0 -- the cleanest possible answer from an instrument that ran nothing. vocabulary_collection caught the retired word CORPUS in my card prose.
think Edited tools/fixtures/t/tools_py_ban_scan.sh while the pass was still running and caught it before the close -- an untracked or modified tracked file enters that runner's tree digest. Parked the patch in .lap/ and restored the tree; the close read tree_moved=no.
think Two candidate refinements both failed on measurement. Reclassifying every cd-relocated dot walk dropped three real findings, since glow_desk_reach and radiant_select_wave cd to the repository root. Spelling ROOT as the root-ish name is the same remembered-name claim the whole reading exists to retire. Neither shipped.
obs A population discovered by walking is a claim about a disk; one discovered by asking git is a claim about the tree. 139 command-position find sites stand in 3,483 tracked tools sources; 44 walk the tree, 17 call git check-ignore, 27 do not, and 18 of those walk a root holding an ignored path on this disk right now.
obs Two numbers because they ask two things. unfiltered reads tracked bytes, so it is identical on every ship and a ceiling over it refuses the same work everywhere. exposed reads this disk, where a peer with an empty .lap/ answers lower for no tree reason, so it is printed by name and gated by nothing. One merged number would have let one checkout's scratch set another ship's ceiling.
obs The repair proved itself on metal rather than by argument. tools_py_ban pruned tools/.cache and tools/.build by name with its reason written beside them, so it had already met this fault and paid for it; git disowns six paths under tools/. A file at tools/bin/probe.py, a room .gitignore names on its own line, makes the elder spelling print TOOLS_PY_BAD and the cure print TOOLS_PY_OK. Four of the six rooms stand absent today, so the fault was latent rather than live.
obs The git-free fallback stays, because that script's upward root walk is deliberately git-free so a copy runs in a pen outside any repository, and a copy reading every path as ignored would refuse nothing. TOOLS_PY_FILTER=git|spelled is printed, since a silent fallback is the fault this repair closes.
obs Four of the twenty-eight are inert members of the gated number and it is said out loud rather than patched away. A ratchet carrying known-unrepairable members is honest; a rule that hides them by guessing is not.
obs The control self-counts, and that is correct. Its pen fixtures are heredocs holding real walks, so they read as sites; the file makes the real call, so they land in git_filtered and never in the gated number. A fixture is part of a tracked source and gets read like one.
obs The scan's own source list reads the INDEX, so the reading changed when the control was staged -- 123 sites to 139. Measured after git add rather than before, the way readme_metrics has to be.
